{
  "_comment": [
    "BleakholdRoyale draft terrain: a 3x3-tile free-for-all battle royale arena (sky drop, shrinking storm,",
    "orbs and loot crates, last player standing). World X is north, Y is west; the block spans X and Y",
    "-1066.67..533.33 with its centre at (-266.67, -266.67). A jittered cliff ring closes the edge, so nobody",
    "walks off the terrain, and every point inside it has ground height (no holes) for the parachute drop.",
    "Landmarks (cover and loot spots, NOT capture bases): the centre ruined keep plateau, a ruined village",
    "(north-west), a watchtower hill (south-west), a crypt hollow (north-east) and a river ford camp",
    "(south-east), with open rolling ground, tree and rock cover between them. The river crosses the eastern",
    "and southern third with two crossings: a shallow ford and a covered bridge.",
    "'pois' are the named points (orb shrines, crate drops, storm centres) written to pois.json for the",
    "server's spawn tables. Chests and orbs themselves are server-spawned GameObjects, NOT terrain doodads;",
    "the terrain only flattens their spots.",
    "Every texture and model path comes from the verified 3.3.5a asset kit (scratchpad assets/kit.json; all",
    "entries live in the base MPQs of a clean client). area_id 5200 is the zone row that package.py adds",
    "(bleakhold_royale.json 'zone.id'; it refuses MCNK area ids it does not add). Placements carry no 'bounds'",
    "here, so MODF extents and chunk",
    "footprints come from each entry's radius (from the kit's footprint estimates); on the VPS, rebuild with",
    "--assets <extracted client files> to take the real model bounds instead."
  ],
